DEMO DIAGNOSTICS
================

The following read-only diagnostic methods exist only when the VMOD was
configured with ``--enable-demo-diagnostics``. A default (production) build
does not expose them.

$Method INT .generation(STRING key)

Return the latest retained hard or soft purge sequence for ``key``. ``0`` means
that no exact purge history is retained for the key, ``-2`` means the sequence
cannot be represented as a VCL integer, and ``-3`` means invalid input.

Automatic sweeps can reclaim entries that no live object needs. When
``purge_history_max_entries`` is non-zero, compaction can also replace exact
per-key history with namespace floors. In either case this diagnostic method
returns ``0`` for a reclaimed key even though a floor can still invalidate old
objects. Disable interval sweeps and use unbounded purge history when exact
per-key diagnostics are required.

Requires ``--enable-demo-diagnostics``.

$Restrict vcl_recv vcl_hit vcl_miss vcl_pass vcl_deliver vcl_synth vcl_backend_fetch vcl_backend_response vcl_backend_error

$Method INT .purge_seq()

Return the namespace's global purge sequence counter: the number of purge
publications accepted since the namespace was created. ``0`` means no purge has
been published yet; ``-2`` means the sequence cannot be represented as a VCL
integer. Reclamation and compaction never lower this value.

Requires ``--enable-demo-diagnostics``.

$Method INT .purgemap_entries()

Return the live purge-map entry count. Certified reclamation removes entries
that no live object needs, so this can drop to ``0`` while namespace floors
still cover the reclaimed history.

Requires ``--enable-demo-diagnostics``.

$Method INT .purgemap_slots()

Return the current purge-map hash-table slot count. ``0`` means no table is
allocated, either because no purge has been published or because reclamation
freed it.

Requires ``--enable-demo-diagnostics``.

$Method INT .purgemap_bytes()

Return the purge-map hash-table size in bytes. ``0`` means no table is
allocated.

Requires ``--enable-demo-diagnostics``.
